<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">These observations do not diagnose the cause. They help keep the conversation focused on the part of the experience that is actually frustrating you.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="restart"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>Try one ordinary restart</h2>
{% call note("care", "Take care", "Restart safely") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Save your work first. If Windows is responding normally, use its usual <strong>Restart</strong> option. After signing in, open only the program you need and note whether the same delay returns. Do not interrupt an update or repeatedly force the computer off to hurry it along.</p>{% endcall %}
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Microsoft lists closing unused apps and restarting among its performance suggestions. It also identifies startup apps, limited storage, outdated software and older hardware as possible contributors to poor performance. Its guidance explains how to review startup apps in Task Manager. See <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/experience/performance-optimization/tips-to-improve-pc-performance-in-windows">Microsoft’s Windows performance guidance</a>.</p>
{% call note("care", "Take care", "Look before changing anything") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">If you do inspect startup apps, start by looking. Do not disable an unfamiliar item simply because it appears in the list, and do not disable security tools. Note what you recognise and ask about anything uncertain.</p>{% endcall %}
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="notes"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span>Make a short before-and-after note</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">You do not need a spreadsheet or specialist software. A few lines are enough:</p>
{% call note("info", "Try this", "Describe the waiting") %}
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">After switching on, the sign-in screen appears in about [time]. After signing in, I wait roughly [time] before [ordinary task] works. This started [when]. A normal restart [helped/did not help/I have not tried it]. The message I see is [message, if any].</p>
{% endcall %}
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Approximate timings are useful. The aim is to give someone a repeatable description, not to meet a universal startup-speed target. Avoid comparing your computer with an advertisement or a different machine doing different work.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Also note whether anything changed around the same time: a new program, an update, a new peripheral or a change in how you use the computer. A change is a clue to discuss, not proof that it caused the problem.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="stop"><span aria-hidden="true">04</span>When to stop experimenting</h2>
{% call note("care", "Take care", "Protect access to your files") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">If the computer will not start, important files are inaccessible, or you see an unfamiliar recovery prompt, explain that before arranging a routine performance visit. Do not reset Windows or delete unfamiliar files just to see whether startup improves. Avoid downloading a “speed booster” from a pop-up.</p>{% endcall %}
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">You do not have to diagnose the fault before asking for help. A clear description of the delay is more useful than a list of guesses or changes you cannot undo.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="options"><span aria-hidden="true">05</span>Does slow startup mean you need a new computer?</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Not by itself. The next decision depends on the computer’s condition, the work you need it to do, and what a proposed fix or upgrade would achieve. Our <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://nakedtech.au/guides/slow-computer-fix-upgrade-replace/">guide to fixing, upgrading or replacing a slow computer</a> explains how to compare those options.</p>

